The current implementation uses `manifestEntries.some()` for each story, resulting in O(n*m) complexity. Consider creating a Set of manifest entry IDs before the filter operation for O(n) lookup time, especially if manifestEntries can be large. For example: `const manifestIds = new Set(manifestEntries.map(e => e.id))` then use `manifestIds.has(story.id)`.
```suggestion
  const manifestIds = new Set(manifestEntries.map((entry) => entry.id));

  return Object.entries(csf._stories)
    .filter(([, story]) =>
      // Only include stories that are in the list of entries already filtered for the 'manifest' tag
      manifestIds.has(story.id)
```
